{# BJJ Position Hub Page Template #}
{# Generates hub pages with summaries from bottom and top perspectives #}
{# Input: Root fields (name, description, overview, etc.) + bottom_summary, top_summary, slug #}

---
title: "{{ name }} | BJJ Position Guide | BJJ Graph"
description: "{{ description }}"
---

{# PostHog A/B Testing Metadata #}
<body data-content-type="positions-hub" data-sections='["overview","key-principles","variant-comparison","bottom-summary","top-summary","variations-list","related-positions"]'>

{# Debug mode indicator #}
{% if debug_mode %}
<!--
  🐛 BJJ Graph A/B Testing Debug Mode (Hub Page)

  Content Type: positions-hub
  Section Count: 7
  Week Seed: {{ week_seed }}
  Visual Variant: {{ visual_elements }}

  Generated: {{ generation_timestamp }}
-->
{% endif %}

> **Quick Overview**: {{ overview[:200] }}...

---

{# Flexbox wrapper for A/B testing #}
<main class="content-wrapper" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">

<section id="overview" class="content-section">

## What is {{ name }}?

{{ overview }}

</section>

<section id="key-principles" class="content-section">

### Key Principles

{% for principle in key_principles %}
- {{ principle }}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="variant-comparison" class="content-section">

## Position Properties Comparison

{% if variations %}
{# FAMILY: Combined multi-variant table #}

| Variant | Bottom Risk | Top Risk | Bottom Energy | Top Energy | What Makes This Variant Unique |
|---------|-------------|----------|---------------|------------|-------------------------------|
| [[{{ name }}]] | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.risk_level }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.risk_level }} | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.energy_cost }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.energy_cost }} | {{ variant_uniqueness }} |
{% for variant in variants_comparison %}
| [[{{ variant.name }}]] | {{ variant.bottom_risk }} | {{ variant.top_risk }} | {{ variant.bottom_energy }} | {{ variant.top_energy }} | {{ variant.uniqueness }} |
{% endfor %}

{% else %}
{# DUAL: Simple comparison table #}

| Property | Bottom Perspective | Top Perspective |
|----------|-------------------|-----------------|
| Position Type | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.position_type }} |
| Risk Level | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.risk_level }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.risk_level }} |
| Energy Cost | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.energy_cost }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.energy_cost }} |
| Time Sustainability | {{ bottom_summary.state_properties.time_sustainability }} | {{ top_summary.state_properties.time_sustainability }} |

**What Makes This Position Unique:** {{ variant_uniqueness }}

{% endif %}

</section>

<section id="navigation" class="content-section">

## Quick Navigation

### By Perspective
- **[[{{ name }}/Bottom|Bottom Perspective]]** - {% if bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Offensive" %}Sweeps, attacks, and submissions{% elif bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Defensive" %}Escapes, frames, and survival strategies{% else %}Techniques and strategies{% endif %}
- **[[{{ name }}/Top|Top Perspective]]** - {% if top_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Offensive" %}Submissions and positional attacks{% elif top_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Controlling" %}Control, pressure, and dominance{% else %}Techniques and strategies{% endif %}

{% if variations %}
### By Variation
{% for variation in variations %}
- **[[{{ variation.name }}]]** - {{ variation.description }}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

</section>

<section id="bottom-summary" class="content-section">

## {{ name }} Bottom Perspective

{% if bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Defensive" %}
The bottom player in {{ name|lower }} must focus on creating frames, protecting against submissions, and executing systematic escapes to recover guard or better positions.
{% elif bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Offensive" %}
The bottom player in {{ name|lower }} controls the position with offensive attacks including sweeps, submissions, and positional advancements while managing opponent's passing attempts.
{% elif bottom_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Defensive with offensive options" %}
The bottom player in {{ name|lower }} balances defensive frames with offensive opportunities, creating sweeps and submissions when opponent over-commits to passing.
{% else %}
The bottom player in {{ name|lower }} navigates both offensive and defensive opportunities based on opponent's actions.
{% endif %}

### Key Principles

{% for principle in bottom_summary.key_principles %}
- {{ principle }}
{% endfor %}

### Primary Techniques

{% for technique in bottom_summary.offensive_transitions %}
- **[[{{ technique.technique }}]]** → [[{{ technique.target_position }}]]
  - Success Rate: Beginner {{ technique.success_rates.beginner }}%, Intermediate {{ technique.success_rates.intermediate }}%, Advanced {{ technique.success_rates.advanced }}%
{% endfor %}

### Common Errors

{% for error in bottom_summary.common_errors %}
- ❌ **{{ error.error }}**
  - Consequence: {{ error.consequence }}
  - ✅ Correction: {{ error.correction }}
{% endfor %}

👉 **[[{{ name }}/Bottom|Complete Bottom Perspective Guide with Drills and Expert Insights →]]**

</section>

<section id="top-summary" class="content-section">

## {{ name }} Top Perspective

{% if top_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Offensive" %}
The top player in {{ name|lower }} enjoys offensive advantages with access to submissions and positional advancements while maintaining control.
{% elif top_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Controlling" %}
The top player in {{ name|lower }} focuses on maintaining dominant control, applying pressure, and systematically breaking opponent's defensive structure.
{% elif top_summary.state_properties.position_type == "Offensive/Controlling" %}
The top player in {{ name|lower }} balances control maintenance with submission attacks, deciding when to consolidate position versus when to finish.
{% else %}
The top player in {{ name|lower }} manages the position strategically based on opponent's defensive reactions.
{% endif %}

### Key Principles

{% for principle in top_summary.key_principles %}
- {{ principle }}
{% endfor %}

### Primary Techniques

{% for technique in top_summary.offensive_transitions %}
- **[[{{ technique.technique }}]]** → [[{{ technique.target_position }}]]
  - Success Rate: Beginner {{ technique.success_rates.beginner }}%, Intermediate {{ technique.success_rates.intermediate }}%, Advanced {{ technique.success_rates.advanced }}%
{% endfor %}

### Common Errors

{% for error in top_summary.common_errors %}
- ❌ **{{ error.error }}**
  - Consequence: {{ error.consequence }}
  - ✅ Correction: {{ error.correction }}
{% endfor %}

👉 **[[{{ name }}/Top|Complete Top Perspective Guide with Techniques and Expert Insights →]]**

</section>

{% if variations %}
<section id="variations-list" class="content-section">

## Position Variations

{% for variation in variations %}
### [[{{ variation.name }}]]

{{ variation.description }}

[Explore {{ variation.name }} →]({{ slug }}/{{ variation.slug }})

{% endfor %}

</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="related-positions" class="content-section">

## Related Positions

{% for related in related_positions %}
- **[[{{ related.name }}]]** - {{ related.relationship }}
{% endfor %}

</section>

</main>
